Problem Statement

Find the longest string that:

contains only 2 distinct characters
characters should alternate
no same adjacent characters
Input:  "beabeefeab"

Possible valid strings:
"babab" -> length 5
"afafa" -> length 5

Answer = 5
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.Set;

public class TwoCharacters {

    // Check if string is alternating
    public static boolean isValid(String str) {

        for (int i = 1; i < str.length(); i++) {

            if (str.charAt(i) == str.charAt(i - 1)) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }

    public static int alternate(String s) {

        int maxLength = 0;

        // Store unique characters
        Set<Character> uniqueChars = new HashSet<>();

        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            uniqueChars.add(c);
        }

        Character[] chars = uniqueChars.toArray(new Character[0]);

        // Pick every pair
        for (int i = 0; i < chars.length; i++) {

            for (int j = i + 1; j < chars.length; j++) {

                char first = chars[i];
                char second = chars[j];

                StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();

                // Build string using only 2 chars
                for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {

                    if (c == first || c == second) {
                        sb.append(c);
                    }
                }

                String filtered = sb.toString();

                // Check alternating condition
                if (isValid(filtered)) {

                    maxLength = Math.max(maxLength,
                            filtered.length());
                }
            }
        }

        return maxLength;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        String str = "beabeefeab";

        System.out.println(alternate(str));
    }
}
Logic Step-by-Step

For:

beabeefeab

Unique chars:

b, e, a, f

Try all pairs:

b,e
b,a
b,f
e,a
e,f
a,f

For pair (b,a):

Filtered string:

babab

Valid alternating string ✔

Length = 5

Time Complexity

If:

n = string length
k = unique characters

Then:

O(k² * n)

Because:

checking all pairs → k²
scanning string each time → n
